{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"proposed-nomophobic-piranha","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/interfaces/facades cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_attestation_parity_heldout_2e16.py:1-18` — Preserve persisted-attestation parity and deliberate-no-sign behavior. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic.py:168-180,201-205,219-245` — Preserve soft degradation, required inputs, and no-network setup. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py:1-18,132-136` — Preserve store-touching auto-mount and no-store/help non-mutation. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py:1-11` — Preserve observable routing and stream/exit behavior. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py:1-17,36-45,80-90` — Preserve the safe range, deterministic inexact fixture, liveness anchor, and exact digit assertion. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_fsck_structured_326f.py:1-18,120-132,240-245` — Preserve structured completed results, true failures, and separate recovery output. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py:405-414,454-464,499-503,543-548` — Preserve instrument-before-offload, stop-intake, drain-before-exit, and short uvicorn backstop. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py:1-22,170-180,234-243` — Preserve JS-safe encoding, schema allowance, and agreement between response halves. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_read_surface.py:1-17,193-201,259-265,283-304,342-349,421-428` — Preserve lean-field exclusions, wire-size accounting, hard refusal, and valid remedies. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_push_status.py:1-16` — Preserve that caller-visible results must report delivery state because server stderr is invisible. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_stateless_transport.py:21-35` — Preserve that blue-green routing requires stateless HTTP sessions and why graceful retirement cannot rescue old session IDs. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py:1-15,157-160` — Preserve retryability parity and sidecar-loss recovery behavior. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n- `tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py:1-20` — Preserve the CLI/MCP scope, offline seam, exit/schema contract, and default gating. Consumer: comment-hygiene scan only; no exact-text consumer.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_attestation_parity_heldout_2e16.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_central_mount_gate_ad9f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_js_safe_integers.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_fsck_structured_326f.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_list_read_surface.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_push_status.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_stateless_transport.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_plan_review_attestation_facades.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_verify_completion_facades.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"6a8e-7f5b-ea0b-485c","parent_id":"2d43-3c39-307e-4450","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/interfaces/facades"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788571117803828988,"uuid":"266d47ab-d84f-4bd3-b86b-8c7aa13b7872"}